********Lesson Learned*********
1. On end points the spacing does counts  the url wont work
2. Adding comma at the end of the last object key  in postman, it's bug
3. Pgadmin changes named camelcase to be one word unless you use snakecase
4. Cannot POST /rooms is Express saying no route matches. The request never reached your controller. The cause is almost always server.ts
5. const { hotelId, url } = req.body; :: this line uses object destructuring to unpack properties from the incoming request body
6. The Date.prototype.toISOString() JavaScript method converts a Date object into a standardized string format based on ISO 8601
7. The HTTP PATCH method applies partial modifications to an existing resource. Unlike the PUT method, which requires you to send
    a complete, modified version to replace the entire resource
