***** Free points ***** 
Branch Naming Best Practices

• Use a Category Prefix: Start every branch with a clear type to show what kind of work is happening:
	• feature/ or feat/ – For new features or user stories
	• bugfix/ or fix/ – For fixing existing bugs
	• hotfix/ – For urgent fixes pushed directly to production
	• refactor/ – For code restructuring without changing functionality
	• docs/ or chore/ – For documentation or maintenance tasks


.*********************Commit keywords**********************
    • Add: Introduce a new file, function, or resource.
    • Fix: Resolve a broken feature or error.
    • Update: Modify existing functionality or dependencies.
    • Remove: Delete obsolete code, files, or assets.
    • Refactor: Clean up or reorganize code structure.
    • Implement: Build out a specific logic or ticket requirement.
    • Optimize: Improve speed, memory, or execution.


