(node:17736) Warning: SECURITY WARNING: The SSL modes 'prefer', 'require', and 'verify-ca' are treated as aliases for 'verify-full'.
In the next major version (pg-connection-string v3.0.0 and pg v9.0.0), these modes will adopt standard libpq semantics, which have weaker security guarantees.


solution:

    1.net.setDefaultAutoSelectFamilyAttemptTimeout(5000);
      Each attempt now gets 5 seconds instead of 250 ms, which is plenty for a connection from South Africa to the US. This is the line that fixes the problem.

    2.dns.setDefaultResultOrder("ipv4first");
T     his tells Node to try the IPv4 addresses before the IPv6 ones. Your log had ENETUNREACH on an IPv6 address, which means your network has no route for IPv6.



import "dotenv/config";
import dns from "dns";
import net from "net";
import { Pool } from "pg";

// Johannesburg -> Neon (US) is slow: give each connection attempt 5s instead of 250ms
net.setDefaultAutoSelectFamilyAttemptTimeout(5000);
// try IPv4 first, because your network has no IPv6 route
dns.setDefaultResultOrder("ipv4first");

const pool = new Pool({
  connectionString: process.env.DATABASE_URL,
  connectionTimeoutMillis: 30000,
});

export const query = (text: string, params?: any[]) => pool.query(text, params);

export const testDbConnection = async () => {
  try {
    const { rows } = await pool.query(
      "SELECT current_database() AS db, NOW() AS now",
    );
    console.log(`Database connected: ${rows[0].db} at ${rows[0].now}`);
  } catch (error) {
    console.error("Database connection failed:", error);
    process.exit(1);
  }
};


